Andreas, span tags are probably not relevant - they&apos;re really for adding alt text to images for screen readers, but they can be used as a hack to add alt text for unicode symbols which (really) old screen readers don&apos;t recognise. The website you link to gives an example of &quot;â‰¥&quot; having a span tag with &quot;greater than or equal to&quot; as the text. However, we&apos;re trying to extract the Unicode text, not the assistive description of it for a screen reader - we really do want &quot;â‰¥&quot; as the text for that character, not the string &quot;greater than or equal to&quot;.

