Dear Tilman,
I just have make some test. Sorry for the complex example but in the past (dev starts in 2007 !) I need to combine iText and PDFBox to add transparent image in a PDF...
So I have do a more simple example and I found the issue, it is not a ratio problem, but a kind of image not supported by PDFBox after doing a filter on the image. 

So I find a workarround, I will explain it :) !


If i use IText I can write :
{noformat}
	public void applyTransparencyFilter() throws IOException {
		this.bufferedImage = ImageFilterOp.getImageWhiteTransparency(this.bufferedImage);
	}
{noformat}

If I do the same with PDFBox I have a blank image.
=&gt; PDFBox do not deal with Transparency.BITMASK  image

@see in ImageFilterOp.java
BufferedImage out =
			gc.createCompatibleImage(in.getWidth(), in.getHeight(), Transparency.BITMASK);


So I do this workarround, and it works fine now :

{noformat}
	public void applyTransparencyFilter() throws IOException {
		this.bufferedImage = ImageFilterOp.getImageWhiteTransparency(this.bufferedImage);
		// Workarround @see https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PDFBOX-2057
		ByteArrayOutputStream baos = new ByteArrayOutputStream();
		ImageIO.write(bufferedImage, &quot;png&quot;, baos);
		this.bufferedImage = ImageIO.read(new ByteArrayInputStream(baos.toByteArray()));
		System.gc();
	}
{noformat}

